  "raw_label": "1",
  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Shivam Chauhan And 3 Ors. vs State Of U.P. on 21 May, 2020 Author: Rajeev Singh Bench: Rajeev Singh High Court Of Judicature At Allahabad, Lucknow Bench ? In Chamber Case :- Bail No. - 2851 of 2020 Applicant :- Shivam Chauhan And 3 Ors.",
    "facts": "The present bail application has been filed on behalf of the applicants in Case Crime No.119 of 2020 under Sections 188, 269, 270, 271, 273 I.P.C., Section 3 of Epidemic Disease Act, 1897 and Section 51 (56 as wrongly written in the F.I.R.) of Disaster Management Act, 2005, Police Station - Vikas Nagar, District - Lucknow with the prayer to enlarge them on bail.",
    "arguments": "The submission of learned counsel for the applicants are that the applicant is an innocent person and in jail since 17.04.2020. It is further submitted on behalf of the applicant that applicants are running the business of tobacco, Pan Masala etc., having valid licence No. 12716066000427 issued by State Licensing Authority under Food Safety and Standards Act, 2006. He further submitted that on 17.04.2020, police officials taken away entire goods of the applicants without mentioning the Shivam Chauhan And 3 Ors. vs State Of U.P. on 21 May, 2020 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/61253170/ 1 reason and thereafter challaned them in the present case. Learned counsel for the applicants further submitted that except Section 272 I.P.C. all the offences are bailable and it has not been mentioned that which article is adulterated. He further submitted that applicants do not have any criminal antecedents. In these circumstances, the applicants are entitled for bail. In case of being enlarged on bail, they will not misuse the liberty of bail. Learned A.G.A. has opposed the prayer for grant of bail to the applicants and submitted that during the period of Covid-19 Lock Down, the applicant tried to sell the recovered articles but he does not dispute the fact about the valid licence.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "The submission of learned counsel for the applicants are that the applicant is an innocent person and in jail since 17.04.2020. It is further submitted on behalf of the applicant that applicants are running the business of tobacco, Pan Masala etc., having valid licence No. 12716066000427 issued by State Licensing Authority under Food Safety and Standards Act, 2006. He further submitted that on 17.04.2020, police officials taken away entire goods of the applicants without mentioning the Shivam Chauhan And 3 Ors. vs State Of U.P. on 21 May, 2020 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/61253170/ 1 reason and thereafter challaned them in the present case. Learned counsel for the applicants further submitted that except Section 272 I.P.C. all the offences are bailable and it has not been mentioned that which article is adulterated. He further submitted that applicants do not have any criminal antecedents. In these circumstances, the applicants are entitled for bail. In case of being enlarged on bail, they will not misuse the liberty of bail. Learned A.G.A. has opposed the prayer for grant of bail to the applicants and submitted that during the period of Covid-19 Lock Down, the applicant tried to sell the recovered articles but he does not dispute the fact about the valid licence.",
